":"UIT","velden":[{"veld":"regio-links","titel":"","waarde":{"velden":[{"veld":"item-categorie","titel":"Category","waarde":"Upper-level course Bachelor"},{"veld":"item-voertaal","titel":"Instruction language","waarde":"English"}]}},{"veld":"regio-rechts","titel":"","waarde":{"velden":[{"veld":"item-opmerking","titel":"Remark","waarde":"Caution: this information is subject to change"}]}}]},{"rubriek":"rubriek-inhoud","titel":"Aims and content","weergave":"UIT","velden":[{"veld":"item-inhoud-1","titel":"Aims","waarde":"<html>\n<head>\n\t<title></title>\n\t<style type=\"text/css\">body { font-size: 9pt; font-family: Arial } table { font-size: 9pt; font-family: Arial }\n\t</style>\n</head>\n<body>By the end of the course, students will be able to:<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Knowledge</strong>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Use different qualitative and quantitative digital research methods</li>\n\t<li>Understand the strengths and limitations of these methods</li>\n\t<li>Identify ways of combining different methods in a holistic research design</li>\n</ul>\n<strong>Skills</strong>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Use online tools like Communalytic to collect data from social media platforms</li>\n\t<li>Use digital archives like Factiva to collect documents and media reports</li>\n\t<li>Use digital softwares to analyze data collected from these sources</li>\n</ul>\n<strong>Character</strong>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Critically reflect upon their methodological choices and their scientific and societal implications</li>\n\t<li>Understand how they might be able to use digital methods for future academic and professional endeavors</li>\n</ul>\n</body>\n</html>\n"},{"veld":"item-inhoud-2","titel":"Content","waarde":"<html>\n<head>\n\t<title></title>\n\t<style type=\"text/css\">body { font-size: 9pt; font-family: Arial } table { font-size: 9pt; font-family: Arial }\n\t</style>\n</head>\n<body>The course will introduce students to digital methods of data collection, analysis of structured and unstructured data, the strengths and limitations of digital techniques, and how they may be integrated with traditional qualitative and quantitative approaches to cultural research.</body>\n</html>\n"}]},{"rubriek":"rubriek-vrije-velden","titel":"Additional information","weergave":"UIT","velden":[{"veld":"item-vrij-veld-23","titel":"Contact person","gegevenstype":"TEKST","waarde":"<a href=\"https://www.tilburguniversity.edu/nl/medewerkers/s-s-shahin\" target=\"_blank\">dr. S.S. Shahin</a>"}]},{"rubriek":"rubriek-toetsen","titel":"Tests","weergave":"IN","velden":[{"veld":"tabel-toetsen","titel":"Tests","waarde":[{"omschrijving":"Assignments (100%)","samengestelde-toets":"","is_onderliggend_toets":"N","is_bovenliggende_toets":"N","velden":[{"veld":"item-toets-weging","titel":"Test weight","waarde":"100"},{"veld":"item-toets-resultaatschaal","titel":"Grading scale","waarde":"ten points, two decimal places"}]}]}]},{"rubriek":"rubriek-inschrijven","titel":"Course enrolment","weergave":"IN","velden":[{"veld":"tabel-inschrijfperiodes","titel":"Enrolment periods","waarde":[{"omschrijving":"Semester 1","id_cursus_inschrijving":1143772,"velden":[]}]}]},{"rubriek":"rubriek-docenten","titel":"Lecturers","weergave":"IN","velden":[{"veld":"tabel-docenten","titel":"Lecturers","waarde":[{"omschrijving":"Lecturer","velden":[{"docent":"dr. M. Spotti","url_medewerker":"","velden":[]},{"docent":"dr. S.S. Shahin","url_medewerker":"","velden":[]}]}]}]},{"rubriek":"rubriek-materialen","titel":"Materials","weergave":"IN","velden":[{"veld":"tabel-materialen","titel":"","waarde":[]}]}],"hasMore":false,"limit":0,"offset":0,"count":10}